xing  kid-brother type  [Music]  I want a car chicks dig a car titans  pushes against his perception showing a  Robin with a chip on his shoulder to  move out of Batman's shadow and possibly  become his own hero was Nightwing he has  to acknowledge that shadow and wrestle  with it and that's the kind of journey  that can only enfold over a whole season  not just a single one liner the outlaw  one of the most promising things we  learned about Titans at comic-con didn't  show up in the trailer and that's the  involvement of Jason Todd the second DC  Comics character to take up the mantle  of Robin Jason Todd is more popularly  known as a violent hero red hood who  stars in the series Red Hood and The  Outlaws but long before he two-fisted  pistols and ran with the likes of  bizarro Todd was a loyal ally to Batman  a job which ended when he was brutally  but temporarily killed by the Joker  whether you love Jason Todd or hates him  the character is a linchpin in some of  DC's most successful comic-book stories  including death in the family under the  hood and hush he's also another example  of the way in which Batman hangs over  this new series letting lower-tier  characters fight it out in a world  that's already been defined by more  marquee heroes new worlds the thing  about shared universe is you've got to  be pretty careful about not toppling all  the dominoes over every time you add a  new piece Marvel Cinematic Universe now  includes 20 movies and half as many TV  shows restricting the kinds of stories  that can be told at any given moment  DC's own arrow vs. 4 shows under growing  with Constantine getting a retroactive  inclusion Batwoman set to join the  universe and the black lightning just  waiting in the wings for a real  crossover it's a lot to keep in mind for  any screenwriter Titans on the other  hand is new territory as of now we don't  know how Titans will connect to other DC  properties are already exist or if it  even well at all with DC Universe 